sfc3_moment_window_census_macmini_S171.py — bounded-exact census for the
Strong Factorial Conjecture SFC(3) (Edo–van den Essen), all three-slot
supports and shifted windows in the box:

  f = a z^p + b z^q + c z^r,  0 <= p < q < r <= 9   (120 support triples)
  window k in {0,...,6}:  L(f^{k+1}) = L(f^{k+2}) = L(f^{k+3}) = 0 ?
  (L(z^n) = n!)

RESULT:  census done: 840 cells, certified-empty 840, flagged 0: []

Certificate per cell (rigorous, one-way): with degrees (k+1,k+2,k+3) and
D = 3k+4, the Macaulay multiplication matrix {x^alpha F_m} spans the full
degree-D graded piece mod a prime (rank C(D+2,2) over F_p, p in
{1000000007, 998244353, 754974721}); full rank over F_p implies full rank
over Q, hence the ideal contains all degree-D forms and the projective
variety V(F_{k+1},F_{k+2},F_{k+3}) in P^2 is EMPTY over C.  Any common zero
with a zero coordinate is excluded a priori (pure-power moments are nonzero
factorials; two-term vanishing windows of length 3 > 2 contradict the proved
SFC(2)), so emptiness is exactly "SFC(3) holds on this cell".  No cell was
rank-deficient, so no exact escalation was needed.

Controls:
  * smoke boxes (r<=5,k<=3): 80/80 and (r<=4,k<=2): 30/30 certified empty;
  * consecutive supports (p,p+1,p+2), k=0 are re-proved (they are covered by
    the symbolic theorem THM-2812) — census verdicts agree;
  * independent engine: sympy Groebner over QQ with saturation t*abc-1 on the
    non-consecutive shifted cell (p,q,r,k) = (0,2,5,1): reduced basis = [1],
    matching the rank certificate.

Interpretation: SFC(3) — if a 3-term univariate f has 3 consecutive
vanishing factorial power-moments then f = 0 — holds for all supports up to
z^9 and all windows starting at k <= 6.  Complements THM-2812 (all
consecutive supports, first window) in both open directions (arbitrary
supports, shifted windows), each cell with a checkable certificate.

Reproduce:
  python3 04-computation/sfc3_moment_window_census_macmini_S171.py 9 6
